{
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "tests/story_bench.c (make story)",
  "policy": "A relay keeper who reads the gauges, not the code: runs the motor towards the mark until the speed readout reaches 0.28-0.52 c, coasts, and brakes when a rule-of-thumb stopping distance worked out from the wobbling readout reaches the mark (25 % late to 30 % early), 0-3 frames slow; it stops braking when the readout falls below 0.01-0.05 c, then watches the position marker for 0.8-1.6 t: on the mark and still, it waits for the catch arm; still but off the mark, it plans a slow second span; moving, it brakes again. While Kit calls the brake it brakes on her word. On the ford bell it cuts the motor and waits. Its hand comes from the night's own stirred seed, re-drawn per leg. Choices follow the path field.",
  "crisis": "the cell gauge in the red (below 0.25) at any moment in the leg, or a failure (a failure counts as a crisis)",
  "failure": "the cell ran dry (Kit cranks it, or after the cut the turn is lost), the turn ran off the posts or wandered 70 t and was relaunched, or it struck the ford bell's arm",
  "segments": ["to the weir", "to the bell", "back to the gorge", "the water in the hut", "up to the dam road"],
  "note": "16 seeds x 12 nights; every night has its own stirred seed; the path comes from the night number.",
